<title>PHILIPPINES: Asian Dev Bank approves $33 mln loan to Vietnam.</title>
<headline>Asian Dev Bank approves $33 mln loan to Vietnam.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Friday it approved a $33 million-loan to Vietnam for a forestry sector project.</p>
<p>The project would cost a total of $53.2 million and would aim to reforest 114,000 hectares until the mid-2003, ADB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The ADB is financing 62 percent of the project with the Dutch government providing 13 percent and the Vietnam government, 10 percent. The remainder will be contributed by the benficiaries through their labour, the statement said.</p>
<p>The ADB loan carries concessional terms. It is interest-free and is repayable over 40 years, including a grace period of 10 years and a service charge of one percent per year, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
